@page "/docs/components/input-color"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.InputColor
<PageTitle>Input Color - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Input Color</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="input-color" />
        </div>
        <p>An inline color field binding a color string. A swatch dot leads, the text field shows the color in <code>Format</code> and accepts any parseable color, and a trailing button opens the <a href="/docs/components/color-picker">Color Picker</a> in a popup - dragging there writes straight into the field. The color sibling of <a href="/docs/components/input-date">Input Date</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(InputColorUsageExample)"
                Description="Add the using once, then two-way bind a nullable string to Value. Type a color and press Enter, or open the picker." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Basic" Description="The default hex field with a leading swatch and the picker button. Value carries the re-serialized color; null is an empty field."
          Example="typeof(InputColorBasicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Format" Description="Format sets what the field shows and what Value is written in - any of the picker's ten formats. An oklch or oklab value in its own format is kept exactly as authored."
          Example="typeof(InputColorFormatExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Alpha" Description="ShowAlpha serializes transparency and gives the popup an alpha slider; the swatch shows it over a checkerboard."
          Example="typeof(InputColorAlphaExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Swatches and eye dropper" Description="Swatches and ShowEyeDropper flow through to the popup's picker, the same way Min, Max and Culture reach Input Date's calendar."
          Example="typeof(InputColorSwatchesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Format dropdown" Description="ShowFormatPicker adds the dropdown to the popup; switching it converts the value and the field follows. Bind Format to follow along."
          Example="typeof(InputColorFormatPickerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Typed entry" Description="ShowPicker=false leaves the text field alone. It still takes any parseable color - hex without the #, a bare channel list, any color function - and converts it into Format on blur or Enter. Text that does not parse stays in the field flagged invalid until it does; clearing the field clears the value."
          Example="typeof(InputColorTypedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="No swatch" Description="ShowSwatch=false drops the leading dot for a bare field."
          Example="typeof(InputColorNoSwatchExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Programmatic focus" Description="Hold a reference to the component and call FocusAsync to move the keyboard yourself - a shortcut sets the color and returns focus to the field, with Select highlighting the text so it can be typed over at once."
          Example="typeof(InputColorFocusMethodExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Auto focus" Description="AutoFocus focuses the field the moment it appears, ready for typing. BzInputDate has the same parameter."
          Example="typeof(InputColorAutoFocusExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="Disabled greys the field and blocks editing and the popup."
          Example="typeof(InputColorDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Pass your own classes via Class - radius, brand focus ring, or a width the text field grows into."
          Example="typeof(InputColorCustomExample)" />
</div>
